    "body": "Purpose\r\nFixes https://github.com/pytorch/test-infra/issues/8870\r\n\r\nNote an alternative or co-fix is to allow pattern matcher to specialize. https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/pull/200303\r\n \r\nRoot cause. pytorch/pytorch#195383 (\"[inductor]  makes the pattern matcher re-trace each match and require the graph's fake-tensor shapes to equal the re-traced ones, checked with statically_known_true.\r\n\r\n\r\nThe SP pass rewrites x (length s) into all_gather(reduce_scatter(x)). That produces length tp * (s // tp), while downstream nodes keep length s. The two are equal only if s % tp == 0. vLLM guarantees this: _pad_for_sequence_parallelism pads num_tokens to a multiple of TP, and the runner asserts it. But the padding happens before the compiled model runs, so the ShapeEnv never learns the fact and the all-gather + GEMM matches are rejected:\r\n\r\nexpected_meta: unsqueeze val does not match ((1, 2*((s72//2)), 4096), torch.float8_e4m3fn, ...)\r\nFix. After the SP rewrite, record torch._check(size % world_size == 0) on the input of each vllm.reduce_scatter the pass inserted. This adds no assumption beyond what the reduce-scatter rewrite already relies on, and it runs only when SP matched. With the fact recorded, and the diff i landed last week pytorch/pytorch#198808 (\"Restore exact FloorDiv cancellation\") simplifies tp * (s // tp) to s, and the matcher accepts the fusions.\r\n\r\nNote: pytorch/pytorch#195383 is on PyTorch main/nightly and not yet in a release.\r\n\r\nTest Plan\r\npytest -v -s tests/compile/fusions_e2e/test_tp2_async_tp.py \\\r\n  -k \"FLASHINFER and inductor_partition and not +rms_norm and (not +quant_fp8 or +quant_fp8 and (qwen3 or deepseek))\"\r\npytest -v -s tests/compile/passes/distributed/test_sequence_parallelism.py tests/compile/passes/distributed/test_async_tp.py\r\n",
